  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v0.2.0 — Major refactor.\n\nAdded:\n  * Microsoft.Extensions.Logging integration — ILogger<T> resolves from DI and writes through Serilog.\n  * AddLogger(IConfiguration, ...) overload for appsettings.json binding.\n  * Console sink (on by default) and configurable RetainedFileCountLimit (default 31).\n  * Single rolling-file mode is the new default; per-level files are opt-in via SeparateFilesPerLevel.\n  * Global AssemblyVersion enricher (cached, attached to every event).\n  * xUnit test project covering options, DI, and end-to-end writes.\n\nChanged:\n  * No longer mutates global Serilog.Log.Logger — the built ILogger is registered as a DI singleton.\n  * Logger is sealed; ILoggerConfig.Build(options) replaces Configure() (legacy method kept and marked obsolete).\n  * Invariant-culture filenames; output template uses [{Level:u3}].\n  * Stable dependencies pinned: Serilog 4.2.0, Serilog.Sinks.File 6.0.0, Serilog.Sinks.Console 6.0.0, Serilog.Extensions.Logging 9.0.0.\n  * Default MinimumLevel: Verbose -> Information.\n\nBreaking:\n  * Logger.Flush()/FlushAsync() (instance) -> Logger.Shutdown()/ShutdownAsync() (static).\n  * Two-arg Logger constructor removed; only Logger(Serilog.ILogger) remains.\n  * Default file layout is now a single rolling log.txt; set SeparateFilesPerLevel = true to restore the old layout.\n\nFull changelog: https://github.com/IoannTerrible/Serilog.TechTeaStudio.Wrap/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md",
